                "reply_count": 2,
                "retweet_count": 1,
                "source": "Twitter Web Client",
                "text": "President Johnson signed the Food Stamp Act into law in 1964, making the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program (SNAP) permanent. Yet, 61 years later, President Trump has decimated this program as part of his Big Ugly Bill, leaving millions of Americans without food that they rely on. All people in this country need to be supported, not just Trump\u2019s billionaire buddies. I am fighting hard to restore food assistance to those in Washington\u2019s Ninth District and around the nation.",
